From: TactiQ OS <andrey@tactiq.ai>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] corenetwork: declare agentgateway_port_t on TCP 49317

The agentgateway module needs a port type bound to a concrete number so
the in-perimeter MCP listener can bind and nothing else can. Operators
that bind a number to a type (portcon) are rejected by checkmodule in a
loadable module, so the declaration has to live in the base policy.

network_port() declares agentgateway_port_t and generates the matching
corenet_tcp_bind_agentgateway_port() / corenet_tcp_connect_agentgateway_port()
interfaces; the agentgateway module consumes the bind form and
deliberately does not consume the connect form.

49317 is in the IANA dynamic range and collides with nothing already
declared in this file. Note that 49190 -- the number carried by earlier
revisions of the agentgateway recipe and its config -- falls inside the
virt_migration range (49152-49216) and would have been labelled
virt_migration_port_t, denying the bind.

Placed between afs3_callback and agentx to keep the block alphabetical.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TactiQ OS specific service]

Signed-off-by: TactiQ OS <andrey@tactiq.ai>
---
 policy/modules/kernel/corenetwork.te.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/policy/modules/kernel/corenetwork.te.in b/policy/modules/kernel/corenetwork.te.in
--- a/policy/modules/kernel/corenetwork.te.in
+++ b/policy/modules/kernel/corenetwork.te.in
@@ -92,6 +92,7 @@
 network_port(afs_pt, udp,7002,s0)
 network_port(afs_vl, udp,7003,s0)
 network_port(afs3_callback, tcp,7001,s0, udp,7001,s0)
+network_port(agentgateway, tcp,49317,s0)
 network_port(agentx, udp,705,s0, tcp,705,s0)
 network_port(amanda, udp,10080-10082,s0, tcp,10080-10083,s0)
 network_port(amavisd_recv, tcp,10024,s0)
